==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|zickin|zickīn|female kid|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|tikk-īn-|lang=de}} (compare Old English {{term|ticcen||kid|lang=ang}}), from {{proto|Indo-European|digós|goat|lang=de}}, genitive of {{proto|Indo-European|title=|díks|lang=de}}. More at {{l|de|Ziege}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Zicken}}
# [[she-goat]], [[nanny goat]]
# [[bitch]] (arrogant woman)

